<title>INDIA: INDIA FOREX RESERVES RISE TO $29.99 BLN ON AUG 1.</title>
<headline>INDIA FOREX RESERVES RISE TO $29.99 BLN ON AUG 1.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $29.99 billion on August 1, 1997 from $29.69 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Aug 1	 July 25     Aug 2</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     26,030	25,763	17,930</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,924	 3,924	 4,410</p>
<p>    SDRs				    37	     3	    91</p>
<p>    Total			     29,991	29,690	22,431</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
